        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A dehumidifier does help get rid of house centipedes, and it works on two fronts: it dries the air they need and the habitat their prey needs. It works slowly, and it cannot reach the block walls, slabs and drains where they shelter.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Hold 45 to 50 percent with continuous drainage, use sticky traps to find and cut their food supply, and seal drains, sumps, block walls and doors. Keep the machine running every damp season. A few centipedes may still wander in, but a dry, sealed basement with nothing to eat gives them no reason to stay.
          </p>
        </div>

